         "r": "noun"
        },
        {
         "t": "para sa ákin",
         "r": "other"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "note": "(You) Please get my dress. / (You) Please call a doctor for me."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "english",
     "title": "Think of it this way",
     "t": "With a paki- verb the sentence is built around the thing you want done (**ang** aking baró), and the person doing it is shown with **mo**. With a maki- verb the person doing it is the focus (**ka**), and the thing takes **ng**."
    }
   ]
  },
