  {
   "title": "Softening a request: ngâ and namán",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Using either **ngâ** or **namán** signals a request and softens an order, **even without** a paki- or maki- verb."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "What the two words mean",
     "items": [
      "**Ngâ** means *truly* or *indeed*. It shows agreement (**Oô ngâ.** *Yes indeed / of course.*) or emphasis.",
      "**Namán** means many things, including *also*, *too* and *instead*. In a command it does not translate into any particular word, but it softens the request and adds emphasis."
     ]
    },
