     "items": [
      "Paki- verbs are passive (like -in-) and take mo / ko / niyá. Maki- verbs are active (like -um-) and take ka / ako / siyá.",
      "Paki- tenses: pakikúha, pinakikúha, pinakikikúha, pakikikúha. Maki- tenses: makikúha, nakikúha, nakikikúha, makikikúha.",
      "Ngâ or namán after mo softens a request, even with a plain verb: Kúnin mo ngâ ang aking barò.",
      "Ask with Maáarì bang…? and answer Opô, maáarì.",
      "With elders and authorities, use paki- or maki- with pô and polite plural pronouns."
