 "recap": [
  "Say please with a request verb: paki- (passive, doer mo/ko/niyá) or maki- (active, doer ka/ako/siyá).",
  "Paki- verbs are used more, because Tagalogs prefer the passive. The imperative is the form mostly used.",
  "Tenses with kúha: pakikúha, pinakikúha, pinakikikúha, pakikikúha; makikúha, nakikúha, nakikikúha, makikikúha.",
  "Ngâ (truly, indeed) or namán (also, too, instead) softens a request: Kúnin mo ngâ ang aking barò.",
  "Ask with Maáarì bang…? and answer Opô, maáarì (polite) or Oô, maáarì.",
  "With elders and authorities, always use paki- or maki- with pô and polite plural pronouns."
 ]
